{%- comment -%}
  Variant picker — big, honest, decision-friendly option buttons.

  Parameters
    product     product object (required)
    section     section object (required; ids are scoped to section.id)
    variant     the variant to show as selected (required — buy-box works it out:
                ?variant= > merchant's "most chosen" > first available)
    block       optional main-product block (variant_picker) for its settings
    compact     true inside the quick-add drawer
    update_url  true → <variant-picker> writes ?variant= to the address bar

  How each option renders
    size-like   (name contains "size", any case) → a size ladder, smallest
                first when every value is a size (XS < S < M < L < XL…, from
                snippets/size-hints; otherwise in the product's own order).
                Each row: the size's own name in bold ("Large"), the rest of
                the value under it ("91 × 69 × 24cm", or the breeds of
                "Medium: Cocker | Staffie" as "Cocker, Staffie"), the price of
                that size (only when sizes are priced differently), a "Most
                chosen" chip (variant metafield custom.most_chosen or the
                section's most_chosen_value) and a hidden "Recommended for
                Bella" chip that product.js reveals from the Bed Finder result.
                A value with nothing after its name uses the size variant's
                custom.size_hint metafield, and only then (block setting
                show_size_hints, off by default) the store-wide breed/weight
                table — never for a value that carries its own detail.
    colour-like (colour / color) → swatches from the option value's swatch
                (colour or image), else text pills.
    anything else → text pills.
    One value only → a plain "Colour: Herringbone grey" line, no buttons,
                no size guide or finder links.

  Display only (the values used to match variants never change): option
  names "color"/"Color" read "Colour", and all-lowercase values and names
  get a capital ("beige" → "Beige"). Each input carries data-display, which
  product.js shows as the selected value.

  Combinations that don't exist or are sold out stay selectable (you might want
  that colour in another size) but are struck through and announced as such.

  Help sits in the size option's label row, as text links rather than boxes:
    "Size: Medium · Size guide · Not sure? Take the 30-second finder"
  (block settings show_size_guide_link / show_finder_link). Once the Bed
  Finder has a result the finder link becomes "Retake the finder" (product.js
  updateFinderPrompts). The visible row is aria-hidden for its label part; the
  fieldset's legend (visually hidden there) still names the group.

  Without JavaScript the whole picker is hidden (.no-js) and buy-box renders a
  plain <select name="id"> inside the product form instead.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign current = variant | default: product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign has_block = false
  if block.id != blank
    assign has_block = true
  endif

  assign show_hints = false
  assign show_prices = true
  assign show_guide = true
  assign show_finder = false
  assign size_style = 'rows'
  if has_block
    if block.settings.show_size_hints
      assign show_hints = true
    endif
    if block.settings.show_size_prices == false
      assign show_prices = false
    endif
    if block.settings.show_size_guide_link == false
      assign show_guide = false
    endif
    if settings.finder_enable and block.settings.show_finder_link != false
      assign show_finder = true
    endif
    if block.settings.size_style == 'grid'
      assign size_style = 'grid'
    endif
  endif
  if product.price_varies == false
    assign show_prices = false
  endif

  comment
    The option that carries the "Most chosen" / "Recommended" chips: the size
    option, else the first one.
  endcomment
  assign size_idx = -1
  for option in product.options_with_values
    assign oname = option.name | downcase
    if oname contains 'size'
      assign size_idx = forloop.index0
      break
    endif
  endfor
  assign chip_idx = size_idx
  if chip_idx < 0
    assign chip_idx = 0
  endif

  assign mc_list = '|'
  for v in product.variants
    if v.metafields.custom.most_chosen.value == true
      assign mcv = v.options[chip_idx] | downcase | strip
      assign mc_key = '|' | append: mcv | append: '|'
      unless mc_list contains mc_key
        assign mc_list = mc_list | append: mcv | append: '|'
      endunless
    endif
  endfor
  assign mc_setting = section.settings.most_chosen_value | default: '' | downcase | strip
  if mc_setting != ''
    assign mc_list = mc_list | append: mc_setting | append: '|'
  endif

  assign uid = section.id | append: '-vp'
  if compact
    assign uid = uid | append: '-c'
  endif

  comment
    The running offer (snippets/offer): sizes that reach its minimum get a
    quiet "£15 off" beside their price, only where sizes are priced
    differently, and not once the basket already has it (one per order) or
    is over the minimum without it. product.js refreshes the marks.
  endcomment
  capture vp_offer_raw
    render 'offer'
  endcapture
  capture vp_basket_raw
    render 'offer', mode: 'basket', cart: cart
  endcapture
  assign vp_offer = vp_offer_raw | strip | split: '|'
  assign vp_basket = vp_basket_raw | strip | split: '|'
  assign offer_marks = false
  assign offer_min = vp_offer[2] | default: 0 | plus: 0
  if vp_offer[0] == '1' and show_prices
    assign offer_marks = true
    assign vp_basket_sub = vp_basket[1] | default: 0 | plus: 0
    if vp_basket[0] == '1' or vp_basket[3] == '1'
      assign offer_marks = false
    elsif vp_basket_sub > 0 and vp_basket_sub >= offer_min
      assign offer_marks = false
    endif
  endif
  comment
    Only worth marking when some sizes miss the minimum: on a bed where
    every size qualifies the line under the price says it once.
  endcomment
  if product.price_min >= offer_min
    assign offer_marks = false
  endif
  if vp_offer[0] == '1' and show_prices and product.price_min < offer_min
    assign offer_amount_money = vp_offer[1] | default: 0 | plus: 0 | money_without_trailing_zeros
    assign offer_mark_text = 'core.offer.size_mark' | t: amount: offer_amount_money
    assign offer_mark_sr = 'core.offer.size_mark_sr' | t: amount: offer_amount_money
  endif

  comment
    Fit line (Theme settings → Sizing → Measuring rule): a size whose value
    gives the bed's length, like Large · 71 × 58cm, also says it fits dogs
    up to about 51cm: the store's own rule (dog nose to base of tail plus
    20cm is the bed length) worked backwards. Nothing without measurements.
  endcomment
  assign fit_allow = settings.size_fit_allowance | default: 0 | plus: 0
-%}
{%- unless product.has_only_default_variant or product == blank -%}
  {%- if settings.finder_enable -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      The finder's "Recommended for Bella" tag sits on the top edge of its
      size card (product.css), so revealing it never changes a card's height.
      On the bed the stored result points at (html[data-finder-handle], set
      in <head>), the cards are spaced from first paint to make room for it.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- style -%}
      html[data-finder-handle="{{ product.handle | escape }}"] variant-picker[data-product-handle="{{ product.handle | escape }}"] .variant-picker__values--size { row-gap: 0.875rem; padding-top: 0.375rem; }
    {%- endstyle -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  <variant-picker
    class="variant-picker{% if compact %} variant-picker--compact{% endif %}"
    data-product-handle="{{ product.handle | escape }}"
    data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
    data-current-id="{{ current.id }}"
    data-chip-index="{{ chip_idx }}"
    {%- if update_url %} data-update-url{% endif %}
  >
    {%- for option in product.options_with_values -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign idx = forloop.index0
        assign oname = option.name | downcase
        assign kind = 'pill'
        if oname contains 'size'
          assign kind = 'size'
        elsif oname contains 'colour' or oname contains 'color'
          assign kind = 'colour'
        endif
        assign current_value = current.options[idx]

        comment
          The option's display name: "Colour" for color / Color / colour,
          and a capital on an all-lowercase name.
        endcomment
        assign oname_s = oname | strip
        if oname_s == 'color' or oname_s == 'colour'
          assign opt_name = 'product.picker.colour_name' | t
        else
          assign opt_name = option.name | escape
          if oname == option.name
            assign opt_name = option.name | capitalize | escape
          endif
        endif

        comment
          Display text for every value: sizes by their own name (size-hints
          parse: "Large · 91 × 69cm" → "Large" + detail "91 × 69cm"), others
          as typed with a capital when all lowercase. Kept per position as
          label~~detail~~rank in vals_info.
        endcomment
        assign vals_info = ''
        assign sort_keys = ''
        assign all_ranked = true
        assign current_display = current_value
        for value in option.values
          assign v_raw = value.name | default: value | append: ''
          assign v_label = v_raw
          assign v_detail = ''
          assign v_rank = 0
          if kind == 'size'
            capture v_parsed
              render 'size-hints', value: v_raw, mode: 'parse'
            endcapture
            assign vp = v_parsed | split: '|'
            assign v_rank = vp[0] | default: 0 | plus: 0
            assign v_label = vp[2] | default: v_raw | strip
            assign v_detail = vp[3] | default: '' | strip
            if v_rank < 1
              assign all_ranked = false
            endif
          endif
          assign v_lc = v_label | downcase
          if v_lc == v_label
            assign v_label = v_label | capitalize
          endif
          if v_raw == current_value
            assign current_display = v_label
          endif
          assign vals_info = vals_info | append: v_label | append: '~~' | append: v_detail | append: '^^'
          assign v_pos = forloop.index0 | plus: 100
          assign v_key = v_rank | plus: 100 | append: '-' | append: v_pos
          assign sort_keys = sort_keys | append: v_key | append: ','
        endfor
        assign info_list = vals_info | split: '^^'
        assign order_keys = sort_keys | split: ','
        if kind == 'size' and all_ranked
          assign order_keys = order_keys | sort
        endif

        assign values_class = 'variant-picker__values variant-picker__values--' | append: kind
        if kind == 'size'
          assign values_class = values_class | append: ' variant-picker__values--' | append: size_style
        endif
        assign single = false
        if option.values.size == 1
          assign single = true
        endif
      -%}
      {%- if single -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Nothing to choose: say what it is, as a plain line. A one-value
          size reads in full ("One size · 80 × 80cm"); colours as typed.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- liquid
          if kind == 'size'
            assign static_text = current_value
            assign st_lc = static_text | downcase
            if st_lc == static_text
              assign static_text = static_text | capitalize
            endif
          else
            assign static_text = current_display
          endif
        -%}
        <div class="variant-picker__group variant-picker__group--static">
          <p class="variant-picker__static" data-option-static data-option-index="{{ idx }}">
            <span class="variant-picker__name">{{ opt_name }}</span>
            <span class="variant-picker__selected">{{ static_text | escape }}</span>
          </p>
        </div>
        {%- continue -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign has_help = false
        if kind == 'size'
          if show_guide or show_finder
            assign has_help = true
          endif
        endif
      -%}
      <div class="variant-picker__group{% if has_help %} variant-picker__group--help{% endif %}">
      {%- if has_help -%}
        <p class="variant-picker__head">
          <span class="variant-picker__head-label" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="variant-picker__name">{{ opt_name }}</span>
            <span class="variant-picker__selected" data-selected-value>{{ current_display | escape }}</span>
          </span>
          {%- if show_guide -%}
            <span class="variant-picker__help">
              <span class="variant-picker__sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
              <button type="button" class="variant-picker__guide link" data-size-guide-open aria-haspopup="dialog">
                {{- 'product.picker.size_guide' | t -}}
              </button>
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if show_finder -%}
            <span class="variant-picker__help variant-picker__finder" data-finder-prompt>
              <span class="variant-picker__sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
              <span data-finder-prompt-default>
                {{- 'product.picker.finder_question' | t }}
                <button type="button" class="variant-picker__finder-link link" data-open-finder>
                  {{- 'product.picker.finder_cta' | t -}}
                </button>
              </span>
              <span data-finder-prompt-result hidden>
                <button type="button" class="variant-picker__finder-link link" data-open-finder data-finder-step="1">
                  {{- 'product.finder.retake' | t -}}
                </button>
              </span>
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}
      <fieldset
        class="variant-picker__option variant-picker__option--{{ kind }}"
        data-option-index="{{ idx }}"
        data-option-kind="{{ kind }}"
      >
        <legend class="variant-picker__legend{% if has_help %} visually-hidden{% endif %}">
          <span class="variant-picker__name">{{ opt_name }}</span>
          <span class="variant-picker__selected" data-selected-value>{{ current_display | escape }}</span>
        </legend>

        <div class="{{ values_class }}">
          {%- for okey in order_keys -%}
            {%- liquid
              if okey == ''
                continue
              endif
              assign v_i = okey | split: '-' | last | plus: 0 | minus: 100
              assign value = option.values[v_i]
              assign val = value.name | default: value | append: ''
              assign v_info = info_list[v_i] | split: '~~'
              assign disp = v_info[0] | default: val
              assign detail = v_info[1] | default: ''
              assign input_id = uid | append: '-' | append: idx | append: '-' | append: v_i

              comment
                The variant this value would select, keeping the other options
                as they are; else any variant with this value (an available one
                if there is one).
              endcomment
              assign match_v = nil
              assign any_v = nil
              for v in product.variants
                if v.options[idx] == val
                  if any_v == nil
                    assign any_v = v
                  elsif any_v.available == false and v.available
                    assign any_v = v
                  endif
                  assign same = true
                  for o in v.options
                    if forloop.index0 != idx
                      assign co = current.options[forloop.index0]
                      if o != co
                        assign same = false
                        break
                      endif
                    endif
                  endfor
                  if same
                    assign match_v = v
                    break
                  endif
                endif
              endfor
              if match_v
                assign row_v = match_v
              else
                assign row_v = any_v
              endif

              assign state = 'available'
              if match_v == nil
                assign state = 'unavailable'
              elsif match_v.available == false
                assign state = 'sold-out'
              endif

              assign is_mc = false
              if idx == chip_idx
                assign vkey = '|' | append: val | downcase | strip | append: '|'
                if mc_list contains vkey
                  assign is_mc = true
                endif
              endif
            -%}
            <input
              type="radio"
              class="variant-picker__input visually-hidden"
              id="{{ input_id }}"
              name="{{ uid }}-{{ idx }}"
              value="{{ val | escape }}"
              data-value-input
              data-display="{{ disp | escape }}"
              {%- if val == current_value %} checked{% endif %}
            >
            {%- case kind -%}
              {%- when 'size' -%}
                {%- liquid
                  comment
                    The line under the size: the value's own detail, else the
                    size variant's custom.size_hint, else (opt-in) the store
                    table's breeds and weight.
                  endcomment
                  assign h_breeds = ''
                  assign h_weight = ''
                  assign h_own = detail
                  if h_own == ''
                    for v in product.variants
                      if v.options[idx] == val
                        assign mf_hint = v.metafields.custom.size_hint.value | default: '' | strip
                        if mf_hint != ''
                          assign h_own = mf_hint
                          break
                        endif
                      endif
                    endfor
                  endif
                  if h_own == '' and show_hints
                    capture h_breeds
                      render 'size-hints', value: val, mode: 'breeds'
                    endcapture
                    capture h_weight
                      render 'size-hints', value: val, mode: 'weight'
                    endcapture
                    assign h_breeds = h_breeds | strip
                    assign h_weight = h_weight | strip
                  endif
                -%}
                <label
                  class="size-option{% if state != 'available' %} is-unavailable{% endif %}"
                  for="{{ input_id }}"
                  data-value-label
                  data-value="{{ val | escape }}"
                >
                  <span class="size-option__main">
                    <span class="size-option__top">
                      <span class="size-option__value">{{ disp | escape }}</span>
                      {%- if idx == chip_idx -%}
                        {%- if is_mc -%}
                          <span class="size-option__chip size-option__chip--popular" data-most-chosen-chip>{{ 'product.picker.most_chosen' | t }}</span>
                        {%- endif -%}
                        <span class="size-option__chip size-option__chip--match" data-recommended-chip hidden>
                          {%- render 'icon', name: 'paw' -%}
                          <span data-finder-name="{{ 'product.picker.recommended' | t }}">{{ 'product.picker.recommended_default' | t }}</span>
                        </span>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </span>
                    {%- liquid
                      assign fit_cm = 0
                      if fit_allow > 0 and detail != ''
                        capture fit_len
                          render 'size-hints', value: val, mode: 'length'
                        endcapture
                        assign fit_len = fit_len | strip | plus: 0
                        if fit_len > 0
                          assign fit_cm = fit_len | minus: fit_allow
                        endif
                      endif
                    -%}
                    {%- if h_own != '' -%}
                      <span class="size-option__hint">
                        {{- h_own | escape -}}
                        {%- if fit_cm >= 20 -%}
                          <span class="size-option__fit">
                            <span aria-hidden="true"> · {{ 'product.picker.fit' | t: cm: fit_cm }}</span>
                            <span class="visually-hidden">. {{ 'product.picker.fit_sr' | t: cm: fit_cm }}</span>
                          </span>
                        {%- endif -%}
                      </span>
                    {%- elsif h_breeds != '' or h_weight != '' -%}
                      <span class="size-option__hint">
                        {{- h_breeds -}}
                        {%- if h_breeds != '' and h_weight != '' %} · {% endif -%}
                        <span class="size-option__weight">{{ h_weight }}</span>
                      </span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </span>
                  <span class="size-option__end">
                    {%- if show_prices and row_v -%}
                      <span class="size-option__price" data-value-price>{{ row_v.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                    {%- if offer_mark_text and row_v -%}
                      <span class="size-option__offer" data-offer data-offer-promo data-value-offer data-min="{{ offer_min }}"{% unless offer_marks and row_v.price >= offer_min %} hidden{% endunless %}>
                        <span aria-hidden="true">{{- offer_mark_text -}}</span>
                        <span class="visually-hidden">{{ offer_mark_sr }}</span>
                      </span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                    <span class="size-option__state" data-value-state data-visible-state>
                      {%- if state == 'sold-out' %}{{ 'product.buy.sold_out' | t }}{% elsif state == 'unavailable' %}{{ 'product.buy.unavailable' | t }}{% endif -%}
                    </span>
                  </span>
                </label>
              {%- when 'colour' -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign swatch_style = ''
                  assign has_swatch = false
                  if value.swatch.image
                    assign sw_url = value.swatch.image | image_url: width: 96
                    assign swatch_style = 'background-image: url(' | append: sw_url | append: ');'
                    assign has_swatch = true
                  elsif value.swatch.color
                    assign swatch_style = 'background-color: ' | append: value.swatch.color | append: ';'
                    assign has_swatch = true
                  endif
                -%}
                {%- if has_swatch -%}
                  <label
                    class="swatch-option{% if state != 'available' %} is-unavailable{% endif %}"
                    for="{{ input_id }}"
                    data-value-label
                    data-value="{{ val | escape }}"
                    title="{{ disp | escape }}"
                  >
                    <span class="swatch-option__swatch" style="{{ swatch_style }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span class="visually-hidden">{{ disp | escape }}</span>
                    <span class="visually-hidden" data-value-state>
                      {%- if state == 'sold-out' %}, {{ 'product.picker.sold_out' | t }}{% elsif state == 'unavailable' %}, {{ 'product.picker.unavailable' | t }}{% endif -%}
                    </span>
                  </label>
                {%- else -%}
                  <label
                    class="chip pill-option{% if state != 'available' %} is-unavailable{% endif %}"
                    for="{{ input_id }}"
                    data-value-label
                    data-value="{{ val | escape }}"
                  >
                    <span class="pill-option__text">{{ disp | escape }}</span>
                    <span class="visually-hidden" data-value-state>
                      {%- if state == 'sold-out' %}, {{ 'product.picker.sold_out' | t }}{% elsif state == 'unavailable' %}, {{ 'product.picker.unavailable' | t }}{% endif -%}
                    </span>
                  </label>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- else -%}
                <label
                  class="chip pill-option{% if state != 'available' %} is-unavailable{% endif %}"
                  for="{{ input_id }}"
                  data-value-label
                  data-value="{{ val | escape }}"
                >
                  <span class="pill-option__text">{{ disp | escape }}</span>
                  {%- if idx == chip_idx and is_mc -%}
                    <span class="pill-option__chip" data-most-chosen-chip>{{ 'product.picker.most_chosen' | t }}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  <span class="visually-hidden" data-value-state>
                    {%- if state == 'sold-out' %}, {{ 'product.picker.sold_out' | t }}{% elsif state == 'unavailable' %}, {{ 'product.picker.unavailable' | t }}{% endif -%}
                  </span>
                </label>
            {%- endcase -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      </fieldset>
      </div>
    {%- endfor -%}
    <p class="visually-hidden" aria-live="polite" data-variant-status></p>
  </variant-picker>
{%- endunless -%}
